          "Rewrite the conv_transpose1d kernel using the scatter approach: for each input position and kernel element, scatter to output position l = i * stride - padding + k + output_padding, with bounds checking. This avoids modulo and negative index complexities, and is numerically equivalent to direct convolution transposed.",
          "Ensure that the output_padding is only applied to the last output index or that the scatter formula includes output_padding appropriately (according to PyTorch, output_padding adds extra size at the end of the output dimension; the scatter approach should incorporate it by simply allowing l up to L_out-1; since L_out already includes output_padding, the scatter condition l < L_out will naturally cover it).",
